# What the container is STARTED with. Copy to docker.env, which docker-compose.yml
# reads and git ignores:
#
#   cp docker.env.example docker.env
#   docker compose up --build
#
# This is not `.env`. That file is Vite's, for development, and is never given
# to the container: a localhost API URL in it would otherwise configure the
# production image.
#
# Every line is optional. A variable that is unset, or set to nothing, keeps
# the value the image was built with. Nothing here is a secret: each value ends
# up in the browser.
#
# No quotes: Compose passes them through as part of the value, and the
# container refuses to start on one. A value may hold letters, digits and
# -_.~:/?#@&+,=% and the title may also hold spaces.

# The API the app calls. An absolute URL, or a same-origin path that the proxy
# in front of the container routes to your backend.
# VUESTRATA_API_URL=https://api.staging.example.com

# VUESTRATA_APP_TITLE=Acme Console

# none | refresh-cookie | session | local
# VUESTRATA_SESSION_PERSISTENCE=refresh-cookie

# VUESTRATA_ERROR_REPORTING_DSN=https://key@o0.ingest.example.com/1
# VUESTRATA_RELEASE=2f1c9ab

# Variables your deploy.config.ts lists under `runtime`, `connectSrcFromEnv` or
# `websocketFromEnv` go here as well.
